<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodelinda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 570–628</span> · Also known as Theodolinda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodelinda was a Bavarian princess who became queen of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a> by marrying King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/authari">Authari</a> in 589 and, after his death, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agilulf">Agilulf</a>. A Catholic who corresponded with Pope <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-i">Gregory the Great</a>, she encouraged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombards">Lombards</a> to move from Arian to Catholic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>. She founded the basilica at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monza">Monza</a>, whose treasury keeps objects linked to her.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodelinda.jpg" alt="Theodelinda" width="320" height="528" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fratelli Zavattari · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Theodelinda_married_Agilulf_(detail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
